WEBVTT

00:00:00.637 --> 00:00:03.583
When your order looks right, it's time to bid.

00:00:03.583 --> 00:00:09.475
"Copy line order" copies your whole ranked order, one line per row, ready to enter yourself.

00:00:09.475 --> 00:00:12.165
It always follows your ranking and tiers —

00:00:12.165 --> 00:00:15.175
not whatever sort you happen to be looking at —

00:00:15.175 --> 00:00:18.121
and leaves out anything you've marked Not bid.

00:00:18.821 --> 00:00:23.831
Or use "Send to VIPS". Choose what happens if none of your lines are left —

00:00:23.831 --> 00:00:26.503
any regular line, secondary, or reserve.

00:00:26.503 --> 00:00:34.518
Answer VIPS's bid questions; nothing is picked for you, but it can tell you what it would answer for this order and why.

00:00:35.218 --> 00:00:42.277
Before you send, it checks your bid — for example, whether you're likely to run out of lines at your seniority —

00:00:42.277 --> 00:00:44.988
and where it has a fix, one tap puts it in.

00:00:45.688 --> 00:00:51.977
Then "Open VIPS and send" opens FedEx's own site with your order filled in. You sign in there —

00:00:51.977 --> 00:00:57.736
Line Select never sees your password, and nothing is sent until you submit it yourself.

